  "term": "intermittent explosive disorder",
  "definition": "Intermittent explosive disorder is a mental disorder marked by repeated episodes of severe aggressive behavior, such as serious assaults or property destruction, caused by difficulty controlling aggressive impulses. The aggression is far greater than the situation would normally provoke and is not better explained by another mental disorder, a medical condition, or substance use.",
